Z||000000||BlackARROW||08-23-2001||12:43 AM||||Yup - I'm still trying to figure out what my kindda Turbo sound (which sounds more like a vacuum shrieking sound that comes out the exhaust pipes).  I have been through many things, from Intake to manifold gasket, to PCV valves.  I just changed my PCV filter, and was looking around to find new stuff.  Looking at the Haynes book, I tried and tested my EGR valve. It seems to work fine, but what doesn't seem good is that I have to vacuum going to it.  Maybe I was thinking, oxide nitrogen exploding could make that vacuum sound.  The thing is I'm losing power when that happens (only happens when riding roughly - after 3000 rpm starting on second gear).  So now what?  My vacuum hose is fine, I don't have vacuum coming from it's plug to the TB.<P>I have good vacuum from the PCV, PCV and filter are new, good vacuum to the Thermac (even though the Thermac valve doesn't work).  <BR>Problem looks like in that plug, going to the EGR. Let's say it's there, can it be clogged somehow, and can it be fixed?<P>My question:  Where is the vacuum coming from?  So I could trace the thing from the source to the problem.  <P>Maybe it won't solve my turbo sound/power loss, but it's just another thing that has to be fixed.<P>Thanks to all<P>Black-&gt;<BR>'85 2m4||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-23-2001||07:45 AM||||It could be your catalytic converter so plugged up, its releasing exhaust from everywhere but the tail pipe.  This will totally choke an engine.<P>The only good cat is a hollow one.<BR>EPA Come get me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||BlackARROW||08-23-2001||09:53 AM||||I thought of that one in the first place, but I have no more cat   *big smile*.<P>Does the EGR vacuum come from the manifold?<BR>Maybe it be the result of air going it from the gasket? doing that crazy "..wwwooooooooOOOOOOOO" sound at high rpm. Causing at the same time that "no vacuum" to that valve?  I have to find that major vacuum leak.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||falconhulk||08-23-2001||10:09 AM||||From what I can tell by tracing that vacum line the EGR seems to get its vacum from the right side of the manifold.  I maybe wrong as I only looked for 3 minutes and it was getting dark<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/i-4_b_l.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||08-23-2001||11:04 AM||||You're right...the control solinoid is on the pass side, a line runs under the plenum to the valve.  Then there is a tube that goes from under the valve to the plenum(likes to leak, cause high idle see other threads).<P>This noise only happens at high rpm?  You got me.  See how much exhaust is coming out.  Rev the engine and feel the exhaust coming out.  There is a slim chance that the baffles in the muffler have collapsed blocking flow...probably not though.<P>Shooting in the dark here- without hearing it!!!||||reg||1
