Z||000008||BlackARROW||08-24-2001||01:32 AM||||I've looked and realised something.  The EGR solenoid is only on the V6, right?  I was looking, but couldn't find anything that could look like it.  Sure it's not the MAP sensor.<P>I have a Negative Backpressure kindda EGR.  I have read that somehow, the engine creates that vacuum (so where is that connection to the plenum valve for the EGR?)  Still no vacuum at all from that particular plenum valve. Is there any other things that could cause a defective EGR system other than "high idling" ?<P>For my crazy TURBO sound, it looks like there is something in the muffler. It stumbles sometimes very slightly on idle.  Could that come from the manifold gasket?  But if I would have a leak there, probably I would have more problems at all rpm range, so my muffler is gone.  Hehe. 8)  It is weird though - it happens when I press on the gas pedal big time, and reving like 3-4k.  That's why I keep thinking of "too much gas" somewhere and blablabla.. <P>Thanks a lot.<P>Black-&gt;<BR>'85 2m4 (200,000 km - wooo!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||4
